+    // (and any pending invocations) until nothing can make further progress, then copies the main
+    // thread's context back into the runtime so the driver's own context is current again.
+    // stepBudget bounds it, so a guest that blocks forever cannot hang the driver.
+    // Returns true if anything was run.
+    bool serviceInvocations(int stepBudget = 4096);
+    // Undo an inline attempt that was aborted. Unused now that overrides stay deferred; retained
+    // because it is the only correct way to restore a thread whose wait was registered by guest
+    // code that must be re-run, and the next attempt at synchronous overrides will need it.
+    void rollbackAbortedInlineInvocation(int threadId);
