+    // as "must only be caught at EeScheduler::run()". A driver that is not the scheduler -- which
+    // is exactly what tools/harness/vulcan4_harness.cpp is -- catches it itself, so the throw
+    // leaves the guest's callee frame, the queued invocation is never serviced, and the guest's
+    // own caller-saved registers never get the handler's result. GT4's syscall-override
+    // convergence loop is shaped exactly like the caller below, and its $s2/$s3 were observed
